This idea would probably be very hard to implement, because of all the
different special cases for artifacts in the code. But it would be
interesting....

Have a random artifact designed at game start, by taking all the things
that all the artifacts do and choosing some of them at random.
Obviously not all are equal, so maybe assign points to the qualities
available and choose randomly that way.

So, in one game there might be a Fooblitsky staff artifact, which has a
chance of blinding enemies, confers hungerless regeneration and is +2
against trolls.

This random artifact could replace one of the standard artifacts, or be
in addition to it ... patch designer would have to decide that.  But a
game without Magicbane but with something else instead could be
interesting....

Another way to do it would be to choose three artifacts at random and
shuffle their attributes ... so you'd have an Magicbane without curse
absorption but with +2 against ogres; a Frostsmasher hammer weapon that
had Frost Brand's cold damage property; and a Blessings Brand long
sword that had curse absorption.

I know this is very poorly thought out, but is there anything here
worth thinking about?



